PART 2: UNDERSTANDING ITEM DELETION
================================================================================

WHAT IS ITEM DELETION?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Deleting an item means removing one grocery record from the state array.

Suppose:

groceryItems = [

  Milk,

  Bread,

  Apples

]


Delete:

Bread


New state:

groceryItems = [

  Milk,

  Apples

]


The original array should NOT be changed directly.


================================================================================
DELETE OPERATION
================================================================================

Suppose Bread has:

id:
'bread-1'


We want to KEEP every item whose ID is NOT:

'bread-1'


Code:

items.filter(
  item =>
    item.id !== id
)


For each item:

Milk:

milk-1 !== bread-1

=
true

KEEP


Bread:

bread-1 !== bread-1

=
false

REMOVE


Apples:

apples-1 !== bread-1

=
true

KEEP


