THE CORE DELETE HANDLER
================================================================================

const handleRemoveItem = (
  id
) => {

  setGroceryItems(
    previousItems =>

      previousItems.filter(
        item =>
          item.id !== id
      )
  )
}


MEMORY:

DELETE FROM ARRAY
      ↓
filter()


================================================================================
LINE-BY-LINE EXPLANATION
================================================================================

+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------+
| CODE                          | PURPOSE                               |
+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------+
| handleRemoveItem(id)          | Receive target ID                     |
| setGroceryItems(...)          | Request state update                  |
| previousItems =>              | Access previous array                 |
| previousItems.filter(...)     | Create filtered array                 |
| item.id !== id                | Keep every non-target item            |
+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------+


================================================================================
WHY USE A FUNCTIONAL SETTER?
================================================================================

Prefer:

setGroceryItems(
  previousItems =>
    previousItems.filter(...)
)


instead of:

setGroceryItems(
  groceryItems.filter(...)
)


because the next list depends directly on the previous list.


This keeps Add, Toggle, and Delete consistent:

ADD:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

setGroceryItems(previous => [

  newItem,

  ...previous

])


TOGGLE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

setGroceryItems(previous =>

  previous.map(...)

)


DELETE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

setGroceryItems(previous =>

  previous.filter(...)

)


