================================================================================
WHY PASS ONLY THE ID?
================================================================================

For deletion, App only needs to know:

WHICH ITEM?


Therefore:

onRemoveItem(
  item.id
)


is generally simpler than passing the whole object:

onRemoveItem(
  item
)


The state owner can identify the record using its stable ID.


================================================================================
CONFIRMATION
================================================================================

This lesson uses:

window.confirm(
  `Delete "${item.name}"?`
)


Possible results:

true

or:

false


If true:

onRemoveItem(
  item.id
)


If false:

return


================================================================================
IS CONFIRMATION REQUIRED?
================================================================================

No.

Confirmation is a product/UX decision.


Useful when:

• Deletion is destructive

• Recovery is difficult

• Accidentally deleting has meaningful consequences


It may be unnecessary when:

• Deletion is easily undoable

• The data is low consequence

• Confirmation causes excessive friction


An Undo pattern can sometimes provide a smoother UX.

For this learning lesson, `window.confirm()` keeps the workflow simple.


